UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Three of Swords represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic De-fragmentation"—the painful, high-intensity phase where the sovereign consciousness is forced to undergo a surgical excision of the delusions, attachments, and heart-based narratives that no longer align with objective reality. Moving beyond the meditative suspension of the Two, the Three signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Cleansing," where the reality-check arrives with undeniable force, piercing the egoic facade. Visually depicted as a heart pierced by three swords against a storm-filled sky, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Integration"—the realization that the pain of the truth is a necessary, diagnostic signal, indicating exactly where your internal architecture is currently misaligned with the manifest world. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Emotional Debugging," where you are being forced to process, acknowledge, and release the data-packets of grief, betrayal, or disappointment that have been accumulating in your system. When the Three of Swords appears, your system is registering a "Crisis-Correction" status; the veil of illusion has been torn, and you are being invited to stop the "grief-loop" of victimhood and instead treat this experience as a brutal, highly accurate diagnostic report. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your vulnerabilities. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Catharsis": allowing the pain to do its work of clearing the field, refusing to suppress the emotional data, and accepting that this rupture is the only way to facilitate the deep, structural healing required for your next, higher-frequency iteration. To inhabit the Three of Swords is to master the art of "Radical Acceptance," recognizing that by facing the raw, piercing truth of your experience without egoic deflection, you are essentially liberating your consciousness from the constraints of the past and preparing it for a reality built on a foundation of absolute, unvarnished honesty.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Three of Swords appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Denial," "Grief-Stagnation," or the catastrophic refusal to integrate the painful data that has been presented to you—a state where you are effectively "masking the wound" while the infection continues to spread through your core operating system. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "suppression" with "resilience," even as you realize your internal operating system is in a state of terminal, unmanaged emotional entropy. You are essentially "bleeding in silence," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to "not be affected" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually process the trauma. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "unflappable agent," while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of bitterness, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency resentment, the experience of "toxic stagnation," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your avoidance is the primary cause of your own, systemic decay. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of preservation"; you are obsessively trying to defend against the memory of the rupture, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final resolution is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to open the wound and feel the pain, you would be forced to acknowledge that your previous attachments were fundamentally unsustainable. The reversed Three of Swords exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of "vulnerability," and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the defensive armor and face the heartbreak, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unintegrated self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these suppressive, pain-avoidant scripts, perform a brutal audit of your emotional baggage, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize the integrity of your processing over the comfort of your numbness. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical feeling—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "the mask" over the vulnerability of "the truth," and realizing that until you are willing to let the heart break, release the trapped data, and exist in the raw, unadorned reality of your own, honest recovery, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom numbness you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 31;
